text:
Today’s a big day at #Botany2022!

@evoyeyo is talking in the Spruce- Hilton at 8:15, @the_kunsze at 8:30 in Ballroom E in the convention center, and @L_DBall at 4:45 in Ballroom E. More info below <U+0001F447>.

Be there or be square <U+0001F92A> https://t.co/5rHZGACXIJ

retweet_description:
Putnam Fellow at @ArnoldArboretum of Harvard University.
Plant cold hardiness, fruit crops, plant ecophysiology.
@UWMadison alumni. <U+0001F3F3><U+FE0F><U+200D><U+0001F308>

text:
@jleebensmack describes efforts to estimate/reconstruct #ancestral #chromosome organization in #MRCA of #angiosperms using #RACCROCHE:
https://t.co/TkW6P1Amvc 

Base chromosome count for ancestral angiosperm seems to confirm longstanding estimates (n=7)  #Botany2022 https://t.co/qgLSNnX4CN

@Barnabas_Daru describes #GreenMaps as a tool to overcome lack of #plant distribution data and understand #biogeographic patterns of plant #diversity worldwide 

Link to preprint: https://t.co/ln58i8cSvA

#Botany2022 https://t.co/qD7nBPX6II

@malia_santos1 examines drivers of #speciation in #african #tropics using Tricalysia as a model

Dated phylogeny w/ #A353 bait set loci demonstrate both Fragmentation-#refugia &amp; #ecotones hypotheses help explain #diversification in different clades

#Botany2022 https://t.co/Yt4hPLB5BI

@erikarmoore11 has a QR code link to her amazing talk (&amp; more) resolving relationships in #Packera (#Compositae) w/ #phylogenomics

#Morphology and #ploidy apparently not phylogenetically conserved, but a strong signal of geographic structure

#Botany2022 https://t.co/WE7NirNvfU https://t.co/cRwJV50IuQ

@plantbotsci solving a mystery in #Ipomoea - I. Carolina morphotype resembles I. grandifolia, are they the same thing &amp; just geographically disjunct? Turns out they are same!

Interested in #Convovulaceae? Join the @convolv_network @laeserman @anaritagsimoes 

#Botany2022 https://t.co/2SuZYoPW99

@Glossopetalon talking about antiracism was on point! <U+0001F525>

All the talks were great at the Black Botanical Legacy: Fostering a Community of Equity in Botanical Science symposium. Thank you for your hard work #BlackBotanistsWeek 
 #Botany2022

